    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1644">

                <pb facs="1349" n="1233" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1233"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.74/13.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Secretary of the
                        Navy</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-04-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 15, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence, I
                    have the honor to enclose herewith, for your information, a copy of a memorandum
                    by the Solicitor of this Department, dated April 4, 1912, dealing with the
                    subject of our treaty right to establish wireless telegraph stations not only in
                    the Canal Zone but on the Isthmus of Panama itself, and to inquire whether it is
                    your desire that this Department now proceed to notify the Panaman Government of
                    the purpose of the Government of the United States, in accordance with the
                    rights granted by treaty, to acquire sites for wireless stations at the points
                    indicated in your communication of January 23, 1912, and to take steps to obtain
                    the necessary control of these sites.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
